============================================================
PHASE 2 — FIX OLLAMA CLOUD SUPPORT
==================================

The current system may treat Ollama as local-only. That is incomplete.

NaySchool must support both:

A. Local Ollama:
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_API_KEY=

B. Ollama Cloud:
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com
OLLAMA_API_KEY=<user_key>

Update configuration so `.env.example` includes:

APP_NAME="NaySchool 3.0"
APP_ENV=development
APP_DEBUG=true
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./nayschool.db
SECRET_KEY=change-this-secret-key
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=10080

DEFAULT_AI_PROVIDER=auto
ALLOW_CLOUD_AI=true

OLLAMA_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_DEFAULT_MODEL=llama3.2

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
OPENROUTER_DEFAULT_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat

DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_DEFAULT_MODEL=deepseek-chat

CORS_ORIGINS=[http://127.0.0.1:8000,http://localhost:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000,http://localhost:8000)

Important:

* Do NOT create a real `.env` file with keys.
* Do NOT hardcode API keys.
* Ensure `.env` is in `.gitignore`.
* Ensure `.env.example` has blank placeholders only.

Update `backend/config.py`:

* Add OLLAMA_API_KEY if not already present.
* Ensure pydantic-settings reads it properly.
* Keep existing settings compatible.

Update `backend/ai/providers/ollama_provider.py`:

Behavior:

* Always call:
  {OLLAMA_BASE_URL}/api/chat

* If OLLAMA_API_KEY exists and is not empty, send:
  Authorization: Bearer <OLLAMA_API_KEY>

* If OLLAMA_API_KEY is empty, send no Authorization header.

* Use:
  stream=false

* Use async httpx.

* Add timeout handling.

* Return normalized response:

{
"provider": "ollama",
"model": "...",
"content": "...",
"raw": {...}
}

Update `/api/ai/health`:

It should report something like:

{
"providers": {
"ollama": {
"configured": true,
"base_url": "...",
"mode": "local" or "cloud",
"api_key_present": true or false
},
"openrouter": {...},
"deepseek": {...}
}
}

Do not expose actual key values.

Update README.md and docs/AI_PROVIDER_PLAN.md:

* Say local Ollama requires no key.
* Say Ollama Cloud uses OLLAMA_API_KEY.
* Give both examples.

============================================================
PHASE 3 — ADD DOCUMENT CHUNKS FOR COURSE MATERIALS
==================================================

NaySchool currently supports file upload, but it needs course memory.

Add a new SQLAlchemy model:

DocumentChunk:

* id: int primary key
* course_file_id: foreign key to CourseFile
* course_id: foreign key to Course
* chunk_index: int
* content: text
* created_at: datetime

Relationships:

* CourseFile should have chunks relationship if appropriate.
* Course should have document_chunks relationship if appropriate.

Since this is local MVP, use SQLAlchemy metadata auto-create on startup like the existing app already does.

Update schemas.py:

Add:

DocumentChunkResponse:

* id
* course_file_id
* course_id
* chunk_index
* content
* created_at

CourseSearchRequest:

* query: str

CourseSearchResult:

* chunk_id
* course_file_id
* score
* content

CourseSearchResponse:

* results: list[CourseSearchResult]

If the project uses separate schema files, follow the existing style instead of forcing everything into one file.

============================================================
PHASE 4 — ADD FILE TEXT EXTRACTION
==================================

Update pyproject.toml:

Add:

* pypdf

Then use:

uv sync

Supported extraction in this phase:

1. .txt
2. .md
3. .pdf using pypdf

For unsupported files:

* Save the file normally.
* Store metadata normally.
* Return chunk_count = 0.
* Add a friendly message:
  “File uploaded, but text extraction is not supported yet for this file type.”

Supported later, but not now:

* .docx
* .pptx
* images OCR

Add TODOs for them.

Create or update a file parsing service.

Recommended file:

backend/services/document_service.py

Functions:

extract_text_from_file(file_path: str, file_type: str) -> str

Behavior:

* For .txt and .md:
  Read text using utf-8.
  If utf-8 fails, fallback to errors="ignore".

* For .pdf:
  Use pypdf.PdfReader.
  Extract text page by page.
  Join pages with page markers or newlines.
  Handle empty PDFs cleanly.

* For unsupported:
  Return empty string.

Also add:

chunk_text(text: str, max_chars: int = 1000, overlap: int = 150) -> list[str]

Chunking behavior:

* Clean whitespace.
* Keep chunks roughly 800–1200 characters.
* Use overlap so context is not lost.
* Do not create empty chunks.
* Limit extremely huge files for now if needed.
* Add TODO for production-grade chunking later.

Also add:

create_chunks_for_course_file(db, course_file, text) -> int

Behavior:

* Delete old chunks for that file if reprocessing.
* Insert chunks with chunk_index.
* Commit.
* Return number of chunks created.

